    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for the info. The \"72 hours\" thing is a bit intense for a solo operation. You mentioned \"hidden data\" as well—is it really that easy for data to just be lurking around without me knowing? It feels a bit like there are these tiny, invisible things happening in the background of my website that I can't control. How do I make sure nothing \"sneaky\" is happening with my customer files?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand it can seem overwhelming, but protecting data calls for vigilance from both the business owner and a reliable professionals. GDPR also allows for 'pseudonymous data' mixes where some identifying info is altered, which can make the data less sensitive. It might be worth engaging a GDPR consultant or experienced IT specialist who can regularly audit your security measures and practices, helping you identify and strengthen areas that need improvement. Regular sensitivity, security, and transformation (SST) audits can also be useful in maintaining a strong defense against potential breaches.",
